{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1489035-i-now-own-book-1-origin","id":1489035,"title":"I now own Book 1 Origin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-03T17:34:51-07:00","id":1489035,"title":"I now own Book 1 Origin","content":"Yay!, me! I\u2019m really excited by what I\u2019m reading. Even with bare bones rules for Scion characters, ideas are flooding to my imagination.<br /> <br /> A question: is there a Writeup, fanmade or otherwise, dealing with the fictional (even in the real world) gods written by William Blake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T17:48:31-07:00","id":1489036,"title":"","content":"Not that I have seen, but it's fairly easy to suggest new Gods for the game. You want a Scion of Urizen? Propose a Calling and Purview and you're mostly set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T17:58:37-07:00","id":1489037,"title":"","content":"Would the Cthulhu Mythos be Titans or Gods? Or even Primordials?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T18:06:20-07:00","id":1489038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1489035-i-now-own-book-1-origin?p=1489037#post1489037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the Cthulhu Mythos be Titans or Gods? Or even Primordials?</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re getting their own dedicated book as a full fledged pantheon with their own eldritch Scions. IIRC I believe Azathoth is a Primordial and the rest are Gods. They aren\u2019t \u201cTitans\u201d because Titan is a political label with metaphysical consequences because of how Fate responds to narrative. And the Great Old Ones don\u2019t have great enemies ala the Fomorians, Jotuns, Asura etc to fill that niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T19:25:22-07:00","id":1489043,"title":"","content":"The main constant I've noticed in the various &quot;Titans&quot; (I rather wish we'd had a different, not-from-a-specific-pantheon name for them) is that they are usually in some form hostile to their current Pantheon and/or to humanity in general. The ones from the Netjer, for example, include the literal antithesis of Ma'at, the thing that tries to eat the sun every night (and thereby overthrow the pantheon), and the god who tried to make himself the sole member of the pantheon. With the Theoi, they're mainly the loyalists to the old regime which the current pantheon overthrew. With the Deva and the Manitou, theirs tend to be colossal jerks who hate the rest of the pantheon. (In contrast, the Azure Dragon hates the Shen because they've always been colossal jerks to him; I suspect this is a potential plot point if you are playing Scion: Dragon.) <br /> Given the traditional attitudes the Mythos beings have toward humanity, I think you could do an interesting campaign where the PCs are Mythos scions aspiring to become that pantheon's Titans and destroy the existing elder gods and great old ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T19:55:44-07:00","id":1489048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1489035-i-now-own-book-1-origin?p=1489043#post1489043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main constant I've noticed in the various &quot;Titans&quot; (I rather wish we'd had a different, not-from-a-specific-pantheon name for them) is that they are usually in some form hostile to their current Pantheon and/or to humanity in general. The ones from the Netjer, for example, include the literal antithesis of Ma'at, the thing that tries to eat the sun every night (and thereby overthrow the pantheon), and the god who tried to make himself the sole member of the pantheon. With the Theoi, they're mainly the loyalists to the old regime which the current pantheon overthrew. With the Deva and the Manitou, theirs tend to be colossal jerks who hate the rest of the pantheon. (In contrast, the Azure Dragon hates the Shen because they've always been colossal jerks to him; I suspect this is a potential plot point if you are playing Scion: Dragon.)<br /> Given the traditional attitudes the Mythos beings have toward humanity, I think you could do an interesting campaign where the PCs are Mythos scions aspiring to become that pantheon's Titans and destroy the existing elder gods and great old ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an incredibly cool idea.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T15:04:27-07:00","id":1490655,"title":"","content":"I really like how Saints &amp; Monsters articulated Titans, as beings who have lost their connection to humanity with their Legend becoming more about their Purviews than their connection to humanity and human cultures. This can be a consequence of being labeled Titan, and your Legend changing to match, or could be a result of choices and actions of the being in question, with their actions in the World changing their Legend.<br /> <br /> This will <i>usually</i> also mean you're opposed to the current cosmic order, but it lets you have situations where you have Gods who are still metaphysically Gods but labeled Titans, or Titans who are upstanding members of their pantheon they just don't really care about or interact with humanity much and remain metaphysical Titans.<br /> <br /> It also gets weirder when you think about Mantles. Cronus of the Theoi is firmly in the &quot;overthrow the current cosmic order, humanity who?&quot; camp and very securely imprisoned in Tartarus. Saturn, his Roman Mantle (maybe? it's complicated), is an upstanding member of the pantheon with festivals and temples in Rome and is notably not in Tartarus and maybe not even a Titan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T17:34:41-07:00","id":1490661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1489035-i-now-own-book-1-origin?p=1489043#post1489043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main constant I've noticed in the various &quot;Titans&quot; (I rather wish we'd had a different, not-from-a-specific-pantheon name for them) is that they are usually in some form hostile to their current Pantheon and/or to humanity in general. The ones from the Netjer, for example, include the literal antithesis of Ma'at, the thing that tries to eat the sun every night (and thereby overthrow the pantheon), and the god who tried to make himself the sole member of the pantheon. With the Theoi, they're mainly the loyalists to the old regime which the current pantheon overthrew. With the Deva and the Manitou, theirs tend to be colossal jerks who hate the rest of the pantheon. (In contrast, the Azure Dragon hates the Shen because they've always been colossal jerks to him; I suspect this is a potential plot point if you are playing Scion: Dragon.)<br /> Given the traditional attitudes the Mythos beings have toward humanity, I think you could do an interesting campaign where the PCs are Mythos scions aspiring to become that pantheon's Titans and destroy the existing elder gods and great old ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds awesome<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}